<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Jan-June soluble coffee exports below 1996.</title>
<headline>Brazil Jan-June soluble coffee exports below 1996.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exports of Brazilian soluble coffee totaled 23,148 tonnes in first half 1997, a drop of 17.5 percent from 28,058 tonnes in the same period last year, said Brazilian Soluble Coffee Industry Association (ABICS).</p>
<p>Revenue was 26.1 percent lower at $153.13 million against $207.37 million in January to June 1996.</p>
<p>Total soluble coffee exports in 1996 were 58,000 tonnes, down 3.9 percent from 60,365 tonnes in 1995.</p>
<p>ABICS predicts 1997 exports will fall to 57,500 tonnes and total revenue will reach $383.70 million versus $477 million in 1996.</p>
<p>((-- Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 24845417))</p>
